    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How do messages get all the way down to my toes?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Your spinal cord is like a big highway down your back. Messages zoom along it to nerves in your toes.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "The message trip",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🛣️",
            "label": "Spinal cord highway",
            "cue": "spinal"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🦶",
            "label": "Out to your toes",
            "cue": "toes"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So when I want to kick a ball..."
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Your brain sends a message to your leg muscles: kick! And your leg kicks, in a blink.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Kick!",
        "items": [
